            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Elliott pushes for former Ralph Lauren exec. as new Lululemon CEO",
            "description": "<p>As Lululemon (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LULU\">LULU</a>) searches for a new CEO, Elliott Management has taken a $1 billion stake in the athleisure company. The activist investor is pushing for Jane Nielsen, a former Ralph Lauren (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/RL\">RL</a>) executive, to be considered, sources told Yahoo Finance Executive Editor <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brian-sozzi/\">Brian Sozzi</a>.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brooke-dipalma/\">Brooke DiPalma</a>, alongside Slatestone Wealth chief market strategist Kenny Polcari, joins Opening Bid to talk about the CEO shake-up.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/opening-bid/\">Opening Bid</a>.</p>",
